From 99737dbdf57dd62f80646e5de4ed386167bfbc2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:57:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci parity: exact pair/rest contracts, command position, step
 guards, wired suites

Audit findings 1 and 4 (PR #736 review), plus four same-class holes the
audit did not list:

- The differential gates' invocations are now pinned as exact pair/rest
  contracts (_contract_status): every named option must appear with
  exactly its expected values (--file twice, with the two corpora; each
  oracle pin once, with its own value) and the remaining tokens (flags,
  positionals) as an exact multiset. This closes the P1 duplicate-
  override false pass (argparse store is last-wins; asm_option() read
  the first occurrence, so '--objdump <pinned> --objdump objdump'
  validated the pin while running the unpinned tool), the '--32'
  injection on the 64-bit encdiff corpus, unregistered extra tools
  (--objcopy), duplicated corpora, and pin VALUE swaps between --as and
  --objdump (same flat token bag, different pairing). A whole-pair
  REORDER stays legal, as it must (argparse is order-free).

- ensure_gas_invoked resolves COMMAND position (gate/env/VAR= wrappers,
  interpreter) instead of scanning for a token pair anywhere: 'echo
  bash scripts/ensure_gas_247.sh x86_64-linux-gnu', 'false && ...' and
  'if false; then ... fi' no longer count as provisioning. The
  differential-command capture got the same treatment -- a python3 line
  that is the argument of an echo no longer parses as an invocation.

- run_script_bodies drops bodies of steps whose `if:` keeps them off
  the green-path run (anything but always()/success()), and the new
  check_step_guards rejects registered gate commands living in
  conditional steps, under continue-on-error, or under hidden
  LCCC/LCCC_GAS/LCCC_OBJCOPY/LCCC_OBJDUMP env overrides (the argparse
  default channels of the tools under contract).

- check_test_suite_registration (audit finding 4): scripts/test_asmdiff.py
  and 'ensure_gas_247.sh --self-test' must RUN in command position on
  BOTH mirrors, registered as fast local gates -- the 19 + 12 pinned
  contract cases shipped unwired before. Wired into ci_local.sh
  (asmdiff-semantic-validation, gas-oracle-pair-self-test) and the
  hosted 'Verify remaining fast local contracts' step.

- The __main__ block of test_ci_gate_parity.py sat ABOVE
  GateNameUniquenessTest, so direct execution -- the mode CI uses --
  never ran its three tests (24 reported, 27 defined). Moved to the end
  of the module; the suite is 42 tests now, all green.

Validated: check_ci_gate_parity PASS on the real tree; the parity suite
42/42; check_ci_workflow_shell ok; bash -n on both shell files; every
audit mutation (duplicates both spellings both orders, --32 both
directions, --objcopy, duplicate --file, swapped values both mirrors,
echo/false&&/if-false installer decoys, argument-position decoys,
suite-removal, echoed suites) rejected.
